P04.10.04 / P04.07.04 — add the two new consistency checks to the docs gate,
and make the lint and typecheck gates cover scripts/.

This file is founder-only (protected-paths policy), so this session wrote the
change as a patch instead of editing it. Apply it yourself:

    git apply docs/control-plane/patches/0004-p04-gates.patch
    python3 .claude/bin/control_plane_check.py
    python3 .claude/bin/gates.py full

Apply it after patch 0003, which this builds on.

What changes
------------
docs-consistency  gains `check-subprocessors.ts` and `check-brand-strings.ts`.
                  The first ties the subprocessor register to the data-flow
                  diagram, so a provider added three phases from now cannot go
                  unrecorded. The second holds ADR-0034: the brand name is
                  configuration, and DG-00 is still open.

lint              `pnpm turbo run lint` → `pnpm lint`
typecheck         `pnpm turbo run typecheck` → `pnpm typecheck`

The last two are the ones worth reading twice. `turbo run` executes only the
per-package tasks, and `scripts/` is not a package — so the seven consistency
checks and `doctor.ts` were the only code in the repository that no gate linted
or typechecked. The root `lint` and `typecheck` scripts now run turbo and then
cover the root files, and the same change is made in the CI workflow, which had
the identical gap.

Proven rather than assumed: a deliberate `any` and a deliberate type error were
placed in `scripts/`, both passed before the change and both failed after it.

